WEBVTT

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:03.354
This sentence came
in a CSS exam.

00:00:03.394 --> 00:00:04.920
Can you find
the error?

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.070
Most students attack
the verb ‘is’.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.853
But the verb
is fine.

00:00:12.893 --> 00:00:15.476
The real problem
is the word ‘each’.

00:00:16.103 --> 00:00:17.694
‘Each’ means
we pick things

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:18.717
one by one:

00:00:18.757 --> 00:00:20.584
each chair,
each table,

00:00:20.624 --> 00:00:21.691
each sofa.

00:00:21.731 --> 00:00:22.897
So ‘each’ needs
something you

00:00:22.937 --> 00:00:24.109
can count.

00:00:24.737 --> 00:00:26.974
Because furniture
is uncountable.

00:00:27.014 --> 00:00:28.577
It’s not one
object.

00:00:28.617 --> 00:00:29.644
It’s a unit:

00:00:29.684 --> 00:00:31.306
chairs,
tables and sofas

00:00:31.346 --> 00:00:33.854
grouped together
and named as one.

00:00:33.894 --> 00:00:35.182
A unit means one,

00:00:35.222 --> 00:00:36.243
and you can’t
pick ‘each’ out

00:00:36.283 --> 00:00:37.231
of one.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.414
So we give
‘each’ something

00:00:39.454 --> 00:00:40.696
countable to hold:

00:00:40.736 --> 00:00:41.604
a piece.

00:00:41.644 --> 00:00:43.456
Each piece
of furniture.

00:00:44.103 --> 00:00:45.429
‘Each piece
of furniture

00:00:45.469 --> 00:00:47.241
in this display
is on sale for

00:00:47.281 --> 00:00:48.893
half price.’

00:00:49.837 --> 00:00:51.498
Logic, not rules.

00:00:51.538 --> 00:00:53.691
Comment ‘logic’
for the next one.

